Some tasks contain several unrelated color objects, where the output changes only one complete component to another color while preserving the rest. Do not default to template-stamping. First compare each demo input/output exactly, record changed component masks and original/destination colors, then test one consistent selection/recolor rule against all examples. Include object size and relationships to other objects, markers, and dividers in the comparison. Do not infer from color appearance or a single visual resemblance. Request another demo only for a specific unresolved choice that a new example could distinguish; demos cost points. After wrong submissions, reset from exact deltas and reassess the entire rule rather than making small speculative edits.
